---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Website Terms — Unit Alfa"
  description="Use of Unit Alfa’s published component information, photographs, capability specifications and enquiry process."
>
  <PageIntro
    label="WEBSITE INFORMATION"
    title="WEBSITE TERMS."
    intro="Information for component enquiries and supplier discussions. Updated 21 September 2026."
  />
  <article class="container legal-copy section-bottom">
    <h2>Product and capability information</h2>
    <p>
      The website describes Unit Alfa’s published product range and plant profile. Photographs
      illustrate examples; they are not controlled engineering drawings. Generated illustrations are
      labelled. Confirm current equipment availability, material suitability, dimensions, finish and
      manufacturing scope for your part.
    </p>
    <h2>Enquiries and quotations</h2>
    <p>
      Preparing or sending an enquiry is not an order acceptance. Price, tooling, batch size,
      inspection, delivery and commercial terms must be agreed in a written quotation or subsequent
      agreement. No warranty, payment term or delivery commitment is created by this website.
    </p>
    <h2>Certificates and documents</h2>
    <p>
      The ISO 9001:2008 reference is historical. Request current qualification documents directly if
      your procurement process requires them. No current certification is represented here without a
      verified document.
    </p>
    <h2>Photographs and content</h2>
    <p>
      Company photographs are sourced from Unit Alfa’s published website and its Weldtables
      material. Copyright remains with the respective owners. Website access does not grant a right
      to redistribute photographs, drawings or brand assets.
    </p>
    <h2>External services</h2>
    <p>
      Google Maps, YouTube and email services operate independently. Their availability and policies
      apply when you choose to use them.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
